": [4302, 42701]}]}", "latency_ms": 0, "tokens_before": 32506, "tokens_after": 32506, "ok": true, "error": ""}], "final_claim": {"task_id": "t_2025d7ec", "decision": "absent", "mechanism": "cascade", "entities": [798, 131], "window": [4302, 42701], "confidence": 0.9, "evidence": [{"trace_id": "step_01", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_11", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_04", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_13", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_14", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_08", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_05", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_07", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_06", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_09", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_02", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_03", "role": "support"}, {"trace_id": "step_15", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_10", "role": "confounder_control"}, {"trace_id": "step_12", "role": "confounder_control"}], "narrative": "No time-respecting cascade exists from 798 to 131 in [4302, 42701]. Under the required 600-unit inter-event constraint, reachability fails and no temporal paths are found. Critically, the failure persists with unlimited waiting: 798's unconstrained forward cone spans 650 nodes but excludes 131 and all three of its in-neighbours (972, 1877, 1932), so the obstruction is structural rather than a delay-threshold artifact. The tempting confounder is the static 2-hop link through hub 389, but that hub edge is oriented 131->389, so the ignore-time path traverses it against the direction of influence. High ambient volume (4,954 events) and 389's popularity (151 partners) therefore explain the apparent connection without supporting a genuine cascade; 798 itself is nearly inactive with 4 events and out-partners {45, 389}."}, "raw_final_response": "## Conclusion\n\n**Decision: `absent`** \u2014 no time-respecting cascade from 798 to 131.\n\n**Key evidence:**\n\n1. **Direct test fails (step_01):** With the required max_wait \u2264 600, reachability from 798 to 131 returns `reached: false`, having explored only 3 nodes. `temporal_paths` (step_11) returns an empty path set.\n\n2. **Failure is structural, not a wait-limit artifact (step_04, step_13, step_14):** Relaxing max_wait entirely still fails. 798 reaches 650 nodes with unlimited waiting \u2014 a large forward cone \u2014 yet 131 is not among them, nor are *any* of 131's three in-neighbours (972, 1877, 1932). The barrier is edge orientation/ordering, not delay.\n\n3. **The static connection is a confounder, and it is disqualified (step_05, step_07, step_08):** Ignoring time, 798 and 131 appear linked in 2 hops via the mega-hub 389 (151 partners, 170 events \u2014 step_09). But the hub edge runs *131 \u2192 389*, not 389 \u2192 131 (`n_events_u_to_v: 0`, `n_events_v_to_u: 1`). The apparent path traverses that edge backwards, so it can never carry influence toward 131.\n\n4. **Volume/popularity controls (step_02, step_03, step_15):** The window is busy (4,954 events, 1,888 active nodes) and the entity set accounts for 200 events, but 798 itself has only 4 events and 2 out-partners (45, 389). Ambient activity does not create a route.\n\n5. **Direction control (step_10, step_12):** The reverse direction (131 \u2192 798) also fails, and 798 cannot even reach 1932, confirming the negative result is not an artifact of a mis-specified endpoint.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"task_id\": \"t_2025d7ec\",\n  \"decision\": \"absent\",\n  \"mechanism\": \"cascade\",\n  \"entities\": [798, 131],\n  \"window\": [4302, 42701],\n  \"confidence\": 0.9,\n  \"evidence\": [\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_01\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_11\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_04\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_13\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_14\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_08\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_05\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_07\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_06\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_09\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_02\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_03\", \"role\": \"support\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_15\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_10\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"},\n    {\"trace_id\": \"step_12\", \"role\": \"confounder_control\"}\n  ],\n  \"narrative\": \"No time-respecting cascade exists from 798 to 131 in [4302, 42701]. Under the required 600-unit inter-event constraint, reachability fails and no temporal paths are found. Critically, the failure persists with unlimited waiting: 798's unconstrained forward cone spans 650 nodes but excludes 131 and all three of its in-neighbours (972, 1877, 1932), so the obstruction is structural rather than a delay-threshold artifact. The tempting confounder is the static 2-hop link through hub 389, but that hub edge is oriented 131->389, so the ignore-time path traverses it against the direction of influence. High ambient volume (4,954 events) and 389's popularity (151 partners) therefore explain the apparent connection without supporting a genuine cascade; 798 itself is nearly inactive with 4 events and out-partners {45, 389}.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 41658, "total_output_tokens": 3960, "total_tokens": 45618, "total_latency_ms": 56510, "llm_calls": 6, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}